# A repo still on GOPATH-era layout: Go source, no go.mod, no tags. The go tool
# serves it at the repo URL with a HEAD pseudo-version, the same path the tag in
# nogomod.txtar resolves to, so the two cases should agree. A missing go.mod does
# not decide whether a repo is a module.
skip headPseudoVersions has no repo-URL fallback, so a repo with no go.mod yields nothing
repo someorg/nogomodhead
head 110022003300440055006600770088009900aabb 2026-07-08T09:10:11Z
-- someorg/nogomodhead/main.go --
package main

func main() {}
-- want --
someorg/nogomodhead github.fake.test/someorg/nogomodhead v0.0.0-20260708091011-110022003300 2026-07-08T09:10:11Z
